  "notes": "Orientation and touch test for the Freenove FNK0104S (or any touch display wired the same way).\n\nEach corner button, and the centre one, is labelled with where it should be on the picture: TL top left, TR top right, BL bottom left, BR bottom right. Press each: the pressed button is drawn inverted while held, and \"Last pressed\" shows its name (also in the console).\n\nRun it once for each orientation: select the display spi node, set orientation to 0, 90, 180 and 270, deploy, and press all five. Every label must appear where its name says, \"TOP OF PICTURE\" must be at the top as you hold the board, and each button must be the one that answers.\n\nAlso hold a button down: it must stay inverted while held and go back to normal on release, and sliding off before lifting must let it go without sending.\n\nThe display's rotation (how the panel is mounted) is the board's usual 1. The screen is the panel's own size, 320x480, in every orientation."
